I kept processing synchronous because the workload described in the challenge didn't establish a need for durable asynchronous execution. That reduced operational dependencies and allowed me to invest the time in data correctness, automated tests, observability, and deployment. If processing latency or burst volume exceeded the API's latency budget, the next step would be to separate acceptance from processing using a durable queue and worker fleet.
